module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.lowered_output_reread_as_raw_parse_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data lowered_output_reread_as_raw_parse_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "lowered_output_reread_as_raw_parse_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a lowered node that the body-lowering allowlist does not name is RE-READ AS RAW PARSE, and the parse readers' first-match descents answer a PART of it with no diagnostic** (INVALID STATE: a producer's output -- a construct, a field projection, a qualified-name spine, a literal -- reaches a reader above it in v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold, body_lower_is_core_substrate answers false because nobody added that shape to it, and the reader walks the node again as if it were unlowered, answering its first atom, its base, or a recognised descendant.) This is the SOURCE of the silent part-for-whole class that gunbc#12145 exposed site by site (as_cast_has_no_lowered_form, caret_symbol_has_no_lowered_form, else_less_if_statement_has_no_lowered_form and compound_call_argument_value_refused_as_unread all cite 12145's silent narrowing), and each earlier instance was closed at the symptom by growing the allowlist: the qualified-name spine (call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering, gunbc#11683), the construct, the int literal's digit list, and #12269's field projection (`p + g(x).a` lowered to `p + g(x)`). It is DESIGN section 5's absorbing fallback: a reader that cannot classify a node widens to the parse reading instead of refusing.",
    "CENSUS (MQ-5, wise-ant-748, 2026-09-30). Instrument: at each of the nine readers that consult the allowlist and can refuse (operand_ref_read, try_body_lowered, reduce, fold, data_initializer_body, lowered_behind_shells_read, primary_expr, after_children, operator_operand), a node the allowlist rejects that is a non-atom with children and no grammar projection edge refused under a site-named reason, on a scratch pin that never merged; the native route (claim_executor --v2-native-route) ran over the full population beside a baseline at the merge-base. Positive control: the unknown shape refused, a field projection and a raw sequence passed. Result: ZERO sites. Every verdict matched the baseline cause for cause, so the allowlist names every shape today's producers emit. LIMITS, stated with the count: files refused before or during lowering are masked (27 lowering refusals, let_body_not_reachable_from_node and wrapper_retention, can hide a later hit in the same file, so the census is re-measured once those clear); the census keys on the absence of a grammar projection edge. A SEPARATE SITE the nine-reader census could not see, named here per the neat-boar-16 ruling: body_lower_find_core_substrate_optional, a first-match DESCENDANT search whose one caller is body_lower_body_subtree_lower_from_primary. When it meets an unrecognised lowered node it descends and answers the first recognised node inside it, a part for the whole. It is instrumented at its caller by body_lower_find_core_substrate_passes_unrecognised and now refuses there too.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silent wrongness). CURRENT RUNG: structurally guaranteed for the population that reaches the ten sites -- no Accepted program re-reads unrecognised lowered output there, because each refuses with body_lowering_reason_unrecognised_lowered_shape located at the node -- held by a SHAPE test (non-atom, children, no parse projection edge -- the roster is v2.compiler.parse parse_tree_projection_edge, the one authority namespace_graft and symbol_index_fill already ask; the census ran with a ten-label list that also named labels only v2.std.grammar grammar_expr_to_node mints, never parse output, and review 73534 consolidated it onto the roster), not by construction. The refusal names the node and not its producer, because nothing on a Node says which lowering built it. CEILING: structurally impossible. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: EACH BODY-LOWERING PRODUCER DECLARES THE SHAPE IT EMITS AND THE body_lower_is_core_substrate PREDICATE IS DELETED, so no reader classifies a node by shape at all and the hand-synced allowlist no longer decides recognition. STAGING, STATED PLAINLY: this rung keeps that predicate deciding, which departs from the end state of MQ-5 condition (2); the climb here is silent truncation to a located refusal, not construction. The intended realization is a LoweredShape arm returned by each producer by construction and carried in a BodyTerm (RawParse or Lowered) that every reducer consumes, exiting to Node once at the normalize boundary (neat-boar-16 ruling 2026-09-30, option A; a marker edge on Node and a roster-generated predicate were both rejected). The PR that moves the last reducer onto BodyTerm DELETES body_lower_is_core_substrate, body_lower_is_unrecognised_lowered_shape and body_lower_find_core_substrate_optional together; there is no period in which both the predicate and the tag answer for the same reducer. A KNOWN LIMIT OF THE CONTROLS, AND WHY IT IS NOT CLOSED HERE: removing ONE site's guard is not caught, because the guards overlap -- an unknown node the fold no longer refuses still reaches body_lower_reduce, which refuses it -- so the controls establish that the refusal holds, not which site holds it; the mutation that restores the re-read everywhere (the shape test forced false) reds the fold, operand-reader and descendant-search controls while the field projection stays green. The overlap is itself duplicated work (DESIGN section 2): ten sites ask one shape question about one node. It is not pinned site by site, because that would build per-site evidence for guards the cut deletes all together; under BodyTerm a Lowered term is never asked the question at all.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_lowering_unrecognised_lowered_shape", decl_name: "an_unrecognised_lowered_shape_refuses_at_the_fold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_lowering_unrecognised_lowered_shape", decl_name: "the_descendant_search_does_not_answer_a_part_of_an_unrecognised_shape", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_lowering_unrecognised_lowered_shape", decl_name: "a_field_projection_still_lowers_whole", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.value_position_whole_read", decl_name: "a_field_projection_on_a_call_result_in_an_operand_lowers_whole", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
